PERMISSIONS
==============

Subject to Section 3, You are granted the following permissions without charge and without any requirement to seek prior permission.

2.1 Use.

You may download, install, and use Official Releases for any purpose, personal or commercial.

2.2 Servers.

You may install and run Official Releases on any server, public or private, including servers that accept donations, sell access, sell ranks or cosmetic benefits, or are otherwise operated commercially.

The permission granted by this Section concerns AMBUSH only and does not override independently applicable laws, Minecraft terms or usage guidelines, platform terms, or third-party licenses.

2.3 Modpacks.

You may include an Official Release in any Modpack, public or private, free or paid, on any platform.

This permission covers, without limitation:

(a) bundling the AMBUSH jar within a distributable archive;

(b) referencing the AMBUSH project or file through a Modpack manifest;

(c) having the distribution platform or launcher download AMBUSH separately; and

(d) declaring AMBUSH as a dependency rather than including its files.

No credit, attribution, description text, credits entry, or link to any AMBUSH page is required as a condition of this permission.

Credit and links are appreciated but entirely optional.

Automatic listing of AMBUSH by a platform as an included mod or dependency is permitted and creates no additional obligation.

The following do not constitute modification of AMBUSH for the purposes of this License, provided that the contents of the AMBUSH jar itself are not altered:

changing configuration files;

adding, removing, or altering external datapacks or AMBUSH data files;

changing server configuration;

using supported AMBUSH feature toggles; and

applying resource packs.

This permission applies to genuine Modpacks, including Modpacks that are small, niche, centered around AMBUSH, or in which AMBUSH is a major or primary gameplay feature.

This permission may not be used merely as a pretext to redistribute, mirror, sell access to, or place an access barrier around AMBUSH itself.

A distribution is not a Modpack for purposes of this Section where its primary practical purpose is simply to provide the AMBUSH jar rather than to provide a genuine assembled Minecraft modpack or configured gameplay experience.

A Modpack is not disqualified because AMBUSH is prominently featured, is a primary component of the Modpack, or provides a substantial portion of its gameplay.

2.4 Independent Content.

This License claims no ownership of Independent Content merely because that content is designed to work with AMBUSH.

Subject to any rights of third parties in that Independent Content, You may distribute, modify, open-source, sell, include in Modpacks, and license Independent Content on any terms You are otherwise entitled to choose.

2.5 Example Content.

You may copy, modify, and reuse Example Content without restriction under this License, including in Independent Content that You distribute or sell.

Material that is not expressly identified as Example Content remains Protected Material.

2.6 Addons and integrations.

You may create and distribute an Addon, including one that:

depends on AMBUSH;

declares AMBUSH as a dependency;

compiles against the AMBUSH jar;

imports AMBUSH classes where reasonably necessary for that purpose;

calls AMBUSH APIs;

implements AMBUSH interfaces;

references AMBUSH class names, method names, registry identifiers, resource identifiers, event hooks, data formats, or documented integration points;

detects whether AMBUSH is installed; or

otherwise interoperates with or extends AMBUSH.

An Addon must remain a separate project.

This Section does not permit copying substantial AMBUSH implementation code or Protected Material into the Addon.

2.7 Translations.

You may create and distribute translation or localization packs for AMBUSH, and may reproduce the text reasonably necessary to translate or localize AMBUSH.

You may license and distribute Your original translation work on terms You choose, subject to any rights that remain in the underlying AMBUSH text.

This Section does not permit reproduction of AMBUSH documentation or other Protected Material beyond what the translation or localization purpose reasonably requires.

2.8 Media.

You may create, publish, and monetize videos, livestreams, short-form video, screenshots, articles, tutorials, reviews, showcases, wikis, social media posts, and other media featuring AMBUSH.

You may use the AMBUSH name to identify the mod in such media.

2.9 Private modification.

You may decompile, inspect, modify, and patch AMBUSH for Your own private or internal use.

A server operator may run a privately modified build on their own server.

You may not publicly distribute a modified build.

Providing a modified build to players, including where players must receive it in order to connect, constitutes distribution and is not permitted by this Section.

2.10 Examination and interoperability.

To the extent permitted by applicable law, You may examine, decompile, and reverse engineer AMBUSH for the purposes of:

interoperability;

compatibility development;

diagnosing mod conflicts;

debugging;

understanding its APIs; and

Addon development.

This Section does not permit copying substantial implementation code or Protected Material.

Nothing in this License restricts any act that applicable law expressly permits and that cannot lawfully be restricted by agreement.

2.11 Use of the AMBUSH name.

You may use the names "AMBUSH" and "Ambush" descriptively to identify AMBUSH or to indicate a genuine relationship between AMBUSH and Your project, Modpack, datapack, Addon, media, or other content.

Permitted uses include phrases such as:

"an AMBUSH addon";

"AMBUSH Addon";

"for AMBUSH";

"AMBUSH compatibility";

"AMBUSH integration";

"AMBUSH expansion";

"AMBUSH datapack";

"AMBUSH Modpack"; and

comparable descriptive language.

This permission does not transfer ownership of the AMBUSH name and does not authorize copying or use of AMBUSH logos, artwork, or other Protected Material except as otherwise permitted by this License.

For clarity, the permissions in this Section concern the Licensor's use of "AMBUSH" as the identifier of the Licensor's project. They do not grant any permission, license, ownership interest, trademark right, or other right in the third-party names "Create", "Create Aeronautics", or "Aeronautics", or in any third-party logo, artwork, branding, or other identifying material. Any right to use a third-party name or mark must arise independently of this License.

Descriptive use of the AMBUSH name as permitted above does not imply official status, endorsement, or affiliation.

