RESTRICTIONS
===============

Except as expressly permitted by Section 2, and unless separately authorized in writing by the Licensor, You may not:

3.1 Standalone redistribution.

Distribute, publish, mirror, or otherwise make available an Official Release, or any part of it, on a standalone basis.

This includes:

reuploading AMBUSH to another mod site;

uploading it to a file host or mirror;

publishing it through another launcher; and

sharing it from personal file storage.

Distribution as part of a Modpack under Section 2.3 remains permitted.

3.2 Modified versions and forks.

Distribute a modified, patched, or recompiled build of a Covered Version, or publish a fork, continuation, or renamed release substantially derived from a Covered Version, under any name.

3.3 Source code.

Publicly redistribute, publish, or sublicense the source code of a Covered Version, or maintain a publicly distributed independent version of it.

Where the Licensor makes source code for a Covered Version available on a hosting service whose ordinary functionality includes repository forking, use of that built-in functionality as provided by the terms of that service is not itself a breach of this Section.

Such use does not, however, grant any further permission under this License to:

publish releases;

distribute compiled builds;

sublicense the code; or

otherwise distribute the fork.

Nothing in this License is intended to override any mandatory term of such a service.

3.4 Protected Material and misrepresentation.

Copy, extract, translate, or reuse Protected Material in any other project, mod, or product except as expressly permitted by Section 2.

You may not:

represent Yourself as the author or origin of AMBUSH;

represent Your project as the official AMBUSH mod; or

represent an Addon, Modpack, or other content as officially developed, endorsed, or approved by the Licensor when it is not.

Referencing a class name, method name, registry identifier, resource identifier, data format, or other API identifier does not by itself breach this Section.

Incidental or reference use of Protected Material that is reasonably required for compatibility, Addon development, translation, media, Modpack inclusion, or interoperability is permitted to the extent authorized by Section 2.

3.5 Sale of AMBUSH itself.

Sell AMBUSH itself as the product, or place an Official Release behind a payment, subscription, paid download, ad-gate, or comparable access mechanism where AMBUSH itself is what is being provided.

Charging for server access, for a Modpack, for media, or for Independent Content remains permitted under Section 2.

All such activity remains subject to independently applicable laws, Minecraft terms and usage guidelines, platform terms, and third-party licenses.

3.6 Notices.

Remove, alter, obscure, or falsify the copyright, authorship, or license information contained within an Official Release.

You are not required to reproduce this License, or any AMBUSH notice, in Your own Modpack description, credits, or documentation.

Leaving the notices intact within the unmodified Official Release is sufficient.

The permission in Section 1.1 to reproduce the text of this License remains unaffected.

